From ee76e21bcdbb8b83ccc60122ec29c35c7d18b599 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 13:57:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] first boot: retire the setup wizard, ship a real Wi-Fi key,
 warn instead of block

Factory-reset behaviour is rebuilt around a notice rather than a gate. The box
comes up usable on admin/admin, and every admin page carries a banner that
cannot be dismissed until BOTH the login and the Wi-Fi key are changed.

WHY THE GATES GO
Six independent gates forced Reaper_FirstBoot.asp before any page would load:
httpd's request-path gate, get_index_page(), the login-CGI meta refresh, two
state.js redirects, and head guards on the dashboard and the stock password
page. Four of those existed only to plug holes in the others. That design is
what produced the v2.1.2 dual-credential-surface dead-end, the v2.1.6 login
refresh loop and the v2.7.3 BE92U nav flash - six gates had to agree on when
setup was finished and never quite did. All six are gone, and with them
reaper_fbdone, the SSH escape hatch for a gate that no longer exists.

THE FACTORY WI-FI IS NO LONGER OPEN
This is a security improvement, not a relaxation. Factory defaults were
wl_wpa_psk="" with wl_auth_mode_x=open (owe on 6 GHz) - a factory-reset box
broadcast an unprotected network until someone completed the wizard. It now
ships a key on every band: psk2 on 2.4/5 GHz, sae on 6 GHz because the band is
WPA3-only (js/asus.js:1059 deletes the psk family for 6g, and the wireless page
rewrites psk->sae there). wl_crypto tkip+aes -> aes: TKIP is invalid for 11ax/be
and would have capped the radio to legacy rates.

THE BANNER
Reaper_SecBanner.asp is a do_ej fragment, so its strings are resolved
server-side into the user's language (ej.c:108/275) - twelve RSEC_* tokens,
translated in all 25 packs, appended so no existing token's line index moves.
The loader is injected into all four existing blocks plus a new mode 5 for the
three top-level admin surfaces that are skip-listed and would otherwise get
nothing (dashboard, shell, Main_Password).

It cannot be dismissed because there is nothing to dismiss: no control, no
cookie, no client state. Both conditions are recomputed per request, so a
reload, a cleared cookie or a hand-edited DOM all bring it back on the next
page. self!==top keeps a framed page from drawing a second copy.

Never served pre-auth. Main_Login, Nologin, Captive_Portal*, blocking.asp and
the offline/error pages are deliberately excluded - telling an unauthenticated
visitor or a quarantined guest that this router still has factory credentials
hands the fact to exactly the wrong person.

The Wi-Fi condition is a direct PSK comparison (new ej_reaper_wifi_default),
NOT w_Setting. w_Setting means "the wireless page was applied once", so a user
who applied it without touching the password would clear the banner while still
on "admin". Keying a notice's clear-condition off different state than its
fire-condition is the exact shape of the BE92U flash. A radio with an empty key
is not counted as factory, or a box with a radio disabled would nag forever.
The PSK itself never reaches the page; only the boolean does.
